1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:04,760
Okay, male genital system pathology, so we're going to start with the penis.

2
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:09,920
The very first disorder is called hypospadias, and this is when the urethra opens on the

3
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:12,400
inferior surface of the penis.

4
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:16,520
The name tells you a lot about this disorder, hypo means low, so it's on the lower surface

5
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:21,720
of the penis, and it's due to failure of the urethral folds to close, that's particularly

6
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:24,080
high yield for examination purposes.

7
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:27,000
Let's go back and remind ourselves of a little bit of embryology.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Remember that you've got this genital tubercle here, which eventually is going to become

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,440
the glands of the penis or the glands of the clitoris, and then running beneath it, you've

10
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:42,480
got this sort of bulk of tissue called the urethral fold.

11
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:46,880
Now what happens is that as the penis grows out, so imagine that the penis is coming sort

12
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:52,800
of 3D, as it's coming up and out, this urethral fold is going to seal, it's going to zipper

13
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:53,800
up.

14
00:00:53,800 --> 00:01:00,340
And as this zippers up, that then seals the inferior surface of the penis and closes the

15
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:02,120
urethra inside of the penis.

16
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:06,680
If you were looking at it in cross section like this, what you'd actually see is something

17
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:12,760
like this, with these two bumps, let's put an A and a B here, with these two bumps representing

18
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,360
A and B here.

19
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:16,700
And of course this is the urethra here.

20
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:23,100
And so these are going to seal as the glands up here, as this genital tubercle begins to

21
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:24,920
come up and out.

22
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:25,920
And so these should seal.

23
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:29,660
And if they don't seal, then you can imagine that you'd have a hole on the inferior surface

24
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:34,120
of the penis from which urine would come out, and that is called hypospadias.

25
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,920
So that's the first disorder.

26
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:41,860
Again it's important to know for examination purposes, failure of the urethral folds to close.

27
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:43,700
That's particularly high yield.

28
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:48,620
Now epispadias, epi means on top, and so when you have epispadias, you have an opening of

29
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:52,880
the urethra on the superior surface of the penis.

30
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:57,320
This particular disorder is very rare, much more rare than hypospadias, and in this case

31
00:01:57,320 --> 00:02:00,980
you have an abnormal positioning of the genital tubercle.

32
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:05,080
So let's go back and remind ourselves that if the genital tubercle was here, and then you

33
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:10,440
had this urethral fold here, and this was going to go up and out, and then this was going

34
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:15,360
to get the zipper closed, imagine that instead of being up here, the genital tubercle is here.

35
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:21,000
Now as this grows sort of up and out, this gets dragged along the superior surface, and

36
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,540
so now you've got this abnormal opening on the superior surface of the penis.

37
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:29,360
And epi again, very straightforward, epi means on top, so it's going to be on the superior

38
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,360
surface.

39
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:33,280
And this would be due to abnormal positioning of the genital tubercle.

40
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:37,120
So that's a little bit of embryology, but again, examiners love to go after that because

41
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:39,580
that's a great way to test embryology.

42
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:43,500
It's also associated with something called bladder extrophy, and bladder extrophy is when

43
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:49,840
you have opening of the anterior wall of the abdomen at the lower portion above the bladder,

44
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:54,600
such that the bladder wall is also not formed properly, and you get complete exposure of the

45
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,020
bladder wall as well.

46
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:58,720
And that's called bladder extrophy.

47
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,040
The next disorder is condyloma.

48
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:04,220
You're well aware of condyloma from our discussions of the female genital tract, so you can also

49
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:08,560
get a condyloma on the male tract, and just as it would be on the female tract, it's due

50
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,960
to HPV 6 and 11.

51
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:14,920
And in the same way, whenever you have HPV infection, that's always characterized by

52
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,460
coelocytic change.

53
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:21,380
This is the exact same picture that I showed you in the female genital section, and basically

54
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:27,560
I was trying to show you these raisinoid-appearing nuclei, these raisin-appearing nuclei, which indicate

55
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:33,240
coelocytic change, and that's, again, a hallmark of HPV infection.

56
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:38,280
Lymphogranuloma venerium is a necrotizing granulomatous inflammation of the inguinal lymphatics and

57
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,820
the lymph nodes.

58
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:44,020
It's a sexually transmitted disease caused by chlamydia trachomatis, in particular serotypes

59
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:45,620
L1 to L3.

60
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:50,880
Let's just go back and remind ourselves that chlamydia is an obligate intracellular organism.

61
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:54,880
It's not hard to remember because the chlamys, which the word chlamydia comes from, the chlamys

62
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:59,780
is the name of the cloak that was worn by men in ancient Greece, and so it's as if these

63
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:02,640
bugs are cloaked by the cells in which they grow.

64
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:06,340
So anyway, chlamydia is an obligate intracellular organism because it can't make ATP.

65
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:10,560
It needs to steal ATP from the cell, so it can only grow inside another cell.

66
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:14,540
And that's important because when you think about the, when you think about how you're going

67
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:18,840
to make a diagnosis, you need to grow the bug in another cell, so you can grow it in tissue

68
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:23,020
culture of cells, or you can grow it in chick embryo cells, et cetera.

69
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:28,320
It enters mucosal surfaces, generally speaking chlamydia, enters mucosal surfaces as elementary

70
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:33,120
bodies, and then they replicate into something called reticulate bodies, which are then released

71
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:36,120
as more elementary bodies, which can then infect again.

72
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:39,440
And remember that chlamydia trachomatis is divided into several serotypes.

73
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:44,720
So there's A through C, which causes trachoma, there's D through K, which causes urogenital

74
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:48,980
infections and conjunctivitis, and then there's L1 through L3.

75
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:54,840
And L1 to L3, as we're talking about here, that causes lymphogranuloma venerium.

76
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:59,680
Now eventually what happens is that you eventually get healing with fibrosis, but you can get rectal

77
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:03,360
strictures, especially if there's perianal involvement.

78
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:06,540
Squamous cell carcinoma of the penis is a malignant proliferation of squamous cells of

79
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:08,040
the penile skin.

80
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:12,320
The risk factors are going to be the same standard risk factors, in particular high-risk HPV.

81
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:15,740
16, 18, 31, 33, those are your high-risk HPVs.

82
00:05:15,740 --> 00:05:20,140
Two-thirds of squamous cell carcinoma of the penis is due to high-risk HPV.

83
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:24,720
There is also an association with lack of circumcision, and the idea here is that if the patient has

84
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:30,180
foreskin, that can act as anitis for the inflammation and irritation if it's not properly maintained.

85
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:34,460
And so improper maintenance of the foreskin becomes a risk factor.

86
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:38,740
Now there are some precursor lesions to squamous cell carcinoma that are high-yield for exams.

87
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:43,560
Now the first is called Bowen's disease, and the way this presents is in-situ carcinoma.

88
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:46,860
All right, so these are precursor lesions, so they're going to be in-situ carcinoma.

89
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:52,740
So you have in-situ carcinoma that presents as leukoplakia, or a white plaque on the shaft of the penis,

90
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:56,460
and that's called Bowen's disease, so you would do a biopsy, and you would see malignant cells

91
00:05:56,460 --> 00:06:02,060
that have not yet invaded the basement membrane, and that histology is important as well.

92
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:03,960
Erythroplasia of Kuert.

93
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:08,700
This is where the patient has in-situ carcinoma, but instead of presenting as leukoplakia,

94
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:12,740
it presents as erythroplakia, hence the term erythroplasia.

95
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:15,920
And this will also, this would be present on the glands of the penis.

96
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:23,680
So erythroplasia on the glands of the penis, again, it's a precursor lesion to squamous cell carcinoma of the penis.

97
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:27,040
And the third would be something called boanoid papulosis.

98
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:32,140
Now, basically, it's called papulosis because you have little papules, and they tend to be reddish.

99
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:35,760
And it's called boanoid because, like Bowen's disease, there's in-situ carcinoma.

100
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:41,280
However, it's not true Bowen's disease, because in Bowen's disease, that in-situ carcinoma would invade.

101
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:44,720
However, this usually does not progress to invasion, so it's boanoid.

102
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:47,840
It's like Bowen, but it doesn't progress to invasion.

103
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:52,520
So again, boanoid papulosis, reddish papules on the skin of the penis.

104
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:55,900
So that concludes our discussion of penis, and the next topic will be testicle.

